## 5. Output O writeback

Standard fixed-length, non-split prefill uses **TMA store via smem staging**:

```38:38:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/epilogue_fwd.hpp
    static constexpr bool Use_TMA_O = ArchTag::kMinComputeCapability >= 90 && !Varlen && !Split && (!PackGQA || PackGQA_TMA);
```

Path: **accumulator registers → smem_o (STSM/U32x4) → TMA bulk store**:

```258:265:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/epilogue_fwd.hpp
        // Step 1: Write O from rmem -> smem
        if constexpr (Use_smem) {
            auto smem_tiled_copy_O = make_tiled_copy_C(SmemCopyAtomO{}, tiled_mma);
            ...
            cute::copy(smem_tiled_copy_O, taccOrO, taccOsO);
```

```317:331:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/epilogue_fwd.hpp
        if constexpr (Use_TMA_O) {
            ...
                    cute::copy(params.tma_store_O, tOsO, tOgO);
                    tma_store_arrive();
                    tma_store_wait<0>();
```

Fallback to **plain global vectorized stores** when `!Use_TMA_O` (varlen, split, or PackGQA without TMA):

```338:365:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/epilogue_fwd.hpp
        } else {  // Don't use TMA in Varlen case since we don't want to overwrite the output of another sequence
            ...
                flash::copy<...>(gmem_tiled_copy_O, tOrO, tOgO, ...);
```

