## 7. FP8 e4m3 forward at head_dim = 128

### Tile config (prefill, two-level accum, default)

```71:72:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_size.h
            } else if (headdim <= 128) {
                return {128, 192, true, true};
```

→ **128×192**, MmaPV RS, IntraWGOverlap=true.

### V load & transpose

FP8 row-major V triggers in-kernel transpose:

```57:57:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    static constexpr bool Transpose_V = Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor;
```

```183:183:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    // Use LDSM.T and STSM to transpose V in the case of FP8 and V being row-major.
```

Flow:
1. **TMA load V** into `smem_vt` (row layout)
2. Producer WG runs **LDSM.T → byte_perm → STSM_N** into `smem_v` (GMMA-ready layout)

```759:775:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        auto transpose_V = [&](int stage) {
            if constexpr (Transpose_V) {
                ...
                    cute::copy(s2r_tiled_copy_vt, tTranssVt(_, make_coord(_, i), stage), tTransrV);
                    ...
                        tTransrV_64[j].x = __byte_perm(upper, lower, 0x6420);
                        tTransrV_64[j].y = __byte_perm(upper, lower, 0x7531);
                    ...
                    cute::copy(r2s_tiled_copy_v, tTransrV, tTranssV(_, make_coord(_, i), stage));
```

V column permutation is reversed in epilogue on O:

```206:206:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    // Instead we will permute the cols of V, and un-permute the cols of O in the epilogue.
```

Wired via `FP8_TransposeV`:

```36:36:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_launch_template.h
    static constexpr bool FP8_TransposeV = Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor;
```

For FP8 hd128, producer becomes a **full warpgroup** (128 threads) to run transpose:

```124:124:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    static constexpr int NumProducerThreads = !Transpose_V && Use_TMA_KV && Use_TMA_Q ? cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarp : cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup;
```

### PV GEMM: P from registers (RS)

Required for FP8:

```85:87:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    static_assert(!(!MmaPV_is_RS && Is_FP8), "MmaPV must be RS if FP8");
    static_assert(!(!MmaPV_is_RS && Transpose_V), "MmaPV must be RS if Transpose_V");
```

PV GEMM uses `tOrP` (register fragment), not smem P:

```1256:1256:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
                flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/false, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_pv, cute::conditional_return<MmaPV_is_RS>(tOrP, tOsP), tOrV(_, _, _, smem_pipe_read_v.index()), tOrO);
```

Post-softmax, scores get FP8 register permute before PV:

```1230:1233:/home/yak/reference_code/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
            if constexpr (Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor) { flash::permute_Cregs_fp8(tSrS); }
            ...
            convert_type_out(tOrP_acc, tOrP);
```

